# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify SPA history fallback.
#
# Files in public/ are copied verbatim into dist/ by Vite, so this ends up at
# the root of the deployed site where Cloudflare Pages looks for it.
#
# Meaning: for any path that does not match a real file, serve index.html with
# HTTP status 200 (not a redirect — the URL in the address bar is preserved so
# React Router can read it). Without this line, opening /host/events/<id>
# directly returns Cloudflare's 404 page instead of the app.
#
# Real files win: /assets/index-abc123.js is served as itself, because
# Cloudflare Pages checks the filesystem before applying these rules.
#
# The trailing 200 is required. `/*  /index.html  302` would rewrite the URL
# and break every deep link.

/*    /index.html    200
